{
  "why": [
    "The days of a trip, which chat.js::tripDayRows draws on the page and trip_pdf.rs::day_rows prints on paper — two implementations of one rule, with nothing else holding them together. Both test suites read this file, so neither can change what a day means without the other going red.",
    "`rows` is a compact shape: `free N` for a counted run of empty days, and `YYYY-MM-DD:kind@HH:MM,kind` for a day, naming the entries on it in order with the clock each one shows. What an entry says in words is tested on its own side; what is shared here is which days exist, what falls on them, and in what order.",
    "A candidate with no `chosen` and no sibling is the one selected — `selectedCandidate` treats a lone option as the pick, and the Rust side's `selected` agrees."
  ],
